  }
,
  "rationale": "Density, not breadth, is the problem: the feasible front has exactly 1 design (pipelined_m W=25/N=23/ag=2/fg=1/m=6, luts_plus_ffs=2371, power_index=4.46, 59.9 MSPS, err 2^-20.22). unrolled_k reached only 7.79 MSPS max over 30 evals and best accuracy 22.18 bits, so it is throughput-limited and cannot help; iterative (1 micro-rotation/cycle, N+3 cycles/result) is strictly slower than unrolled_k and is therefore provably infeasible on the 50 MSPS constraint, so add_family would only burn budget. That leaves pipelined_m (23/50 feasible, area 2371) and pipelined (6/20 feasible, area 4061) as the only productive families, with pipelined_m dominating on the min-luts_plus_ffs selection rule. I therefore refine inside their observed feasible boxes to (a) test whether shaving data_width (23-24) with more n_iter beats 2371 area while keeping err <= 2^-20, and (b) populate the area vs power_index tradeoff (m 3..8, guards -1..3) so the HV at ref (8000,20) is covered by more than one point. Throughput margin (best seen 158-257 MSPS vs 50 required) means the search can safely trade Fmax/power for area near the 50 MSPS edge."
}

